{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966479,"nonce":"Bi40st10cqSGlgfvzVs/vG8Q6YI=","title":"Mobile browsers: subtree-update jitter on iOS, scroll artifacts on Pixel","message":"Two separate mobile web defects, both P2 — mobile web is a bonus target,\ndesktop Chrome/Edge/Firefox/Safari are primary.\n\n**iPhone 12 Pro Max, Safari / iOS 18+.** Demos render and run, WebGPU\nworks. Stateful subtree updates jitter: accordion open, checkbox toggle\nand similar. The full subtree rebuild plus relayout does not fit a 16ms\nframe on the mobile GPU. Worth trying: separate visual-only prop updates\nfrom structural rebuilds, or defer relayout to the next frame.\n\n**Google Pixel, Chrome Android.** Renders text only, and scrolling\nproduces unbounded artifacts. Suspect a Vulkan/WebGPU driver problem on\nAdreno or Mali, or a surface configuration mismatch — sRGB versus\nnon-sRGB texture format, or an incompatible present mode. Next step is\n`chrome://gpu` diagnostics with the wgpu validation layer enabled.\n\nCarried over from the root `backlog.md`, which this issue replaces.","files":null}]}